---
import Todo from '@/components/ui/Todo.astro';
import { site } from '@/data/site';
import ArticleLayout from '@/layouts/ArticleLayout.astro';

const published = new Date('2026-10-04');
const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'What is the HSN code for a compression spring?',
    a: 'Helical springs of iron or steel are commonly classified under HSN 7320 20. GST is commonly 18%. Confirm the code for your part with your CA.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is a wire form the same HSN?',
    a: 'Not always. A clip or pin that is not a helix may sit under 7326 (articles of iron or steel) rather than 7320. Flag that uncertainty on the PO.',
  },
];
---

<ArticleLayout
  route="hsnGst"
  title="HSN Code for Springs and GST Rate"
  description="HSN 7320 covers springs of iron or steel; 7320 20 covers helical springs. GST is commonly 18%. Confirm with your CA. Wire forms may be 7326."
  h1="HSN code and GST for springs"
  lede="The code buyers put on the purchase order, and the tax rate that usually sits next to it. This is a reading of public tariff pages, not advice from our CA."
  published={published}
  context="a GST invoice"
  takeaways={[
    'HSN 7320 covers springs of iron or steel; 7320 20 covers helical springs.',
    'GST on those headings is commonly 18%.',
    'Wire forms may sit under 7326. Confirm every part with your CA.',
  ]}
  toc={[
    { id: 'codes', text: 'The codes' },
    { id: 'gst', text: 'GST rate' },
    { id: 'wire-forms', text: 'Wire forms' },
    { id: 'sources', text: 'Sources' },
    { id: 'questions', text: 'Questions' },
  ]}
  faqs={faqs}
  related={[
    {
      to: 'springs',
      label: 'Springs we make',
      description: 'The helical springs under 7320 20.',
    },
    { to: 'wireForms', label: 'Wire forms', description: 'Clips, hooks and pins; check 7326.' },
    { to: 'ordering', label: 'Ordering with us', description: 'GST invoice, MOQ, ex-works.' },
    {
      to: 'priceGuide',
      label: 'Spring price guide (India)',
      description: 'What drives cost, not rupee guesses.',
    },
    { to: 'rfq', label: 'Request a quote', description: 'We invoice as RK Enterprises.' },
  ]}
>
  <h2 id="codes">The codes</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>HSN 7320</strong> covers springs of iron or steel. <strong>7320 20</strong> covers
    helical springs — the compression, extension and torsion springs that leave our unit. Stainless
    springs of iron or steel still sit in this family; they are not a separate “SS spring” heading.
  </p>
  <p>
    We invoice as {site.legalName}, GSTIN {site.gstin}. The HSN we print on a given invoice follows
    the part.
    <Todo text="CA confirmation of the HSN we actually print for springs and for wire forms." />
  </p>

  <h2 id="gst">GST rate</h2>
  <p>
    Public guides for HSN 7320 list <strong>GST at 18%</strong>. Treat that as the usual rate, not a
    promise for every part or every year. A concessional or different rate can apply if the
    classification changes.
  </p>

  <h2 id="wire-forms">Wire forms</h2>
  <p>
    A clip, hook or pin that is not a helix may be classified as an article of iron or steel under{' '}
    <strong>HSN 7326</strong>, not 7320. That is uncertain. Do not copy the spring code onto a wire
    form without asking your CA.
  </p>

  <h2 id="sources">Sources</h2>
  <p>Read on 4 Oct 2026, and to be confirmed with a CA:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <a href="https://cleartax.in/s/springs-gst-rates-hsn-code-7320" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        ClearTax: Springs GST rates and HSN 7320
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="https://www.credlix.com/hsn-code/73202000" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        Credlix: HSN 73202000
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a
        href="https://getswipe.in/blog/article/springs-gst-rate-hsn-code-7320-explained-guide-2026"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >
        Swipe: Springs GST guide 2026
      </a>
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    This page is not tax advice. Confirm the final classification of each product with your
    chartered accountant.
  </p>
</ArticleLayout>
